h(2, id: "semantics") { 18. Semantic checks }

p {
    Analysis runs on the document after includes are expanded. The first
    violation stops the build.
}

table {
    row(header: true) {
        cell { Check }
        cell { When it fires }
    }
    row {
        cell { meta title }
        cell { meta is present and has no title field }
    }
    row {
        cell { heading level }
        cell { level is not in 1..6 }
    }
    row {
        cell { empty codeblock / raw / math }
        cell { trimmed content is empty }
    }
    row {
        cell { empty list }
        cell { no items }
    }
    row {
        cell { empty table }
        cell { no rows }
    }
    row {
        cell { empty row }
        cell { no cells }
    }
    row {
        cell { ragged table }
        cell { a row's cell count differs from the first row }
    }
    row {
        cell { image src }
        cell { source string is empty }
    }
    row {
        cell { link URL }
        cell { URL string is empty }
    }
    row {
        cell { include path }
        cell { path is empty or only whitespace }
    }
    row {
        cell { footnote id }
        cell { duplicate definition, or a reference with no definition }
    }
    row {
        cell { list start }
        cell { start is less than 1 }
    }
    row {
        cell { figure src }
        cell { source string is empty }
    }
    row {
        cell { empty deflist }
        cell { no term or desc }
    }
    row {
        cell { details summary }
        cell { summary is missing or empty }
    }
    row {
        cell { cell span }
        cell { colspan or rowspan is less than 1 }
    }
}

p {
    Parse errors are separate: unknown block names, missing braces, bad callout
    types, unclosed raw scopes, unclosed strings, unclosed comments, nesting
    past 64, text after a nested list or nested quote.
}

h(3, id: "diagnostics") { 18.1 Diagnostics }

p {
    Errors print the message, then code{path:line:col}, then the source line and
    a caret. Line and column are 1-based. File errors use distinct text for not
    found and permission denied.
}
